# Public API and release

Canonical guidance: [`.github/contributing.md`](../../.github/contributing.md) (PR guidelines), [`.github/maintenance.md`](../../.github/maintenance.md), [`.github/commit-convention.md`](../../.github/commit-convention.md), package entry points and public types, [`CHANGELOG.md`](../../CHANGELOG.md). External: [vuejs/rfcs](https://github.com/vuejs/rfcs), [vuejs/docs](https://github.com/vuejs/docs), [vuejs/language-tools](https://github.com/vuejs/language-tools) only when the task crosses those boundaries.

## Required

- State whether the change adds API surface, changes common behavior, is breaking, affects types, or needs migration/documentation.
- Recommend `minor` for new API surface and `main` otherwise, but ask a human to confirm before branch mutation or PR preparation.
- Identify evidence for API acceptance or flag missing RFC/maintainer agreement.
- Compare API value against userland alternatives and implementation/size complexity.
- Identify external companion work without silently editing another repository.
- Include compatibility, ecosystem CI, size, and release-note implications in the contribution summary.

## Prohibited

- Do not treat implementation as approval of a new API.
- Do not declare an RFC unnecessary when evidence is ambiguous.
- Do not edit changelog/release files unless the repository's current process and the task explicitly require it.
- Do not publish preview or release packages autonomously.
